  "d2: 🍽️ Mia rests a hand on the pantry door, satisfied. \"No one's going hungry this week. Sitting with the fever cases instead — someone should.\"",
  "d2: 🍽️ Lillian taps the pantry door — full to bursting — and keeps the day's share in hand. \"Dinner's on me tonight, then.\"",
  "d3: 🍽️ Elena eyes the groaning pantry shelves and packs light today. \"No point hauling what'll rot. Mending the nets instead.\"",
  "d3: 🍽️ Elena looks at the full shelves and waves off the day's share. \"No more into the store — we eat at the fire, and the shelves keep.\"",
  "d4: 🍽️ Mia lingers by the full pantry and laughs. \"Full shelves, full bellies. Mending the palisade today — the fence won't fix itself.\"",
  "d4: 🍽️ Elena leaves the surplus by the fire for whoever's hungry. \"The pantry can't take it. We can.\"",
  "d5: 🍽️ DeAndre peeks into the pantry, then turns the foraging party back. \"Plenty for days. Teaching the kids snares instead — they'll need to know.\"",
  "d5: 🍽️ Ingrid leaves the surplus by the fire for whoever's hungry. \"The pantry can't take it. We can.\"",
  "d6: 🍽️ Ingrid stands in the pantry doorway a moment. \"Look at all this. Tending the fire today — someone ought to keep the stories.\"",
